# Project: Steve Meadows — Data Science Portfolio v2

## Overview
Ultra-modern, techie/militaristic data science portfolio website. Dark theme, neon accents, HUD aesthetics, terminal vibes. Built with Next.js, Supabase, Tailwind CSS, and Shadcn/ui. Hosted on Vercel.

## GSD Protocol
This project follows the GSD (Get Stuff Done) protocol. Before writing any code:

1. **Read `plan.md`** — It is the single source of truth for what we're building and the current phase.
2. **Work one phase at a time.** Do not skip ahead or mix phases unless explicitly told to.
3. **Each phase must produce a working state.** No broken builds at the end of a phase.
4. **Mark tasks complete in `plan.md`** by changing `- [ ]` to `- [x]` as you finish them.
5. **If you're unsure, ask.** Don't guess at design decisions or architecture choices.

## Tech Stack (Do Not Deviate)
- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router, NOT Pages Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript (strict mode)
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 + Shadcn/ui
- **Animations:** Framer Motion + CSS animations
- **Database:** Supabase
- **Hosting:** Vercel
- **Fonts:** JetBrains Mono (headings/code) + Inter (body) via `next/font`

## Code Standards

### General
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any` types unless absolutely unavoidable
- Use `const` by default, `let` only when reassignment is needed
- Prefer named exports over default exports
- Keep files focused — one component per file
- Use absolute imports via `@/` path alias

### React / Next.js
- Use Server Components by default; only add `"use client"` when you need interactivity, hooks, or browser APIs
- Use the App Router file conventions: `layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`
- Use `next/image` for all images — never raw `<img>` tags
- Use `next/link` for all internal navigation — never raw `<a>` tags for internal routes
- Use `next/font` for font loading — no external CDN font links
- Colocate components with the routes that use them when they're single-use; shared components go in `src/components/`

### Tailwind CSS
- Use Tailwind utility classes directly — avoid `@apply` except in global base styles
- Use CSS variables for theme tokens (colors, glows) defined in `globals.css`
- Use `cn()` helper (from `lib/utils.ts`) for conditional class merging
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — wrap intense animations in `motion-safe:` variants

### Shadcn/ui
- Install components via CLI (`npx shadcn-ui@latest add <component>`)
- Components live in `src/components/ui/` — do not modify them unless necessary
- Extend Shadcn components by wrapping them, not editing the source

### File Naming
- Components: `PascalCase.tsx` (e.g., `HeroSection.tsx`, `GlitchText.tsx`)
- Utilities/hooks: `camelCase.ts` (e.g., `useScrollProgress.ts`, `cn.ts`)
- Data files: `camelCase.ts` (e.g., `projects.ts`, `skills.ts`)
- CSS files: `kebab-case.css` (e.g., `scan-lines.css`)

## Project Structure
```
src/
  app/                    # Next.js App Router pages
    layout.tsx
    page.tsx
    projects/
      page.tsx
      [slug]/page.tsx
    about/page.tsx
    contact/page.tsx
    not-found.tsx
  components/
    ui/                   # Shadcn/ui components (do not modify)
    layout/               # Navbar, Footer, PageWrapper
    sections/             # Hero, Skills, ProjectsGrid, etc.
    effects/              # Particles, ScanLines, GlitchText, TypeWriter, HUDBracket
  lib/                    # Utilities, Supabase client, helpers
  data/                   # Static data (projects, skills, nav items)
  styles/                 # Global CSS, animation keyframes
```

## Design System

### Colors (CSS Variables)
- `--bg-base`: #0a0a0f (near-black)
- `--bg-surface`: #12121a (card/surface)
- `--bg-elevated`: #1a1a2e (elevated elements)
- `--accent-cyan`: #00f0ff (primary accent)
- `--accent-green`: #39ff14 (secondary accent / success)
- `--accent-amber`: #ffbf00 (warning / highlight)
- `--accent-red`: #ff003c (error / alert)
- `--text-primary`: #e0e0e0
- `--text-secondary`: #888888
- `--text-muted`: #555555

### Glow Effects
Use `drop-shadow` and `box-shadow` with accent colors for neon glow effects. Define reusable Tailwind utilities for these.

### Spacing & Layout
- Max content width: 1200px centered
- Section padding: `py-20 md:py-32`
- Consistent spacing scale via Tailwind defaults

## Design Personality
- **DO:** Dark, tactical, futuristic, clean, high-contrast, purposeful animations
- **DON'T:** Cluttered, cartoonish, pastel, over-animated to the point of distraction
- Think: military command center + cyberpunk terminal + clean modern portfolio
- Every visual effect should serve a purpose — atmosphere, hierarchy, or feedback
- Animations should feel snappy and intentional, not floaty or slow

## Performance Rules
- Lighthouse target: 90+ on all metrics
- Lazy load below-the-fold content
- Use `next/image` with proper `width`/`height` or `fill` — no layout shift
- Keep client-side JS minimal — Server Components first
- No massive dependencies for small features (don't import all of D3 for one chart)

## Git Conventions
- Branch per phase: `phase-1/scaffolding`, `phase-2/visual-system`, etc.
- Commit messages: concise, imperative mood (e.g., "Add glitch text component", "Wire up navbar links")
- Commit working states — don't commit broken code

## When In Doubt
1. Check `plan.md` for the current phase and task list
2. Keep it simple — don't over-engineer
3. Ship working code, then iterate
4. Ask before making architectural decisions not covered in the plan
